      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-303981",
      ":question/problem": "A car dealership has $24$ vehicles available. The table below shows the distribution of vehicles by type and whether they are priced above or below $$25,000$.\n\n| Type | Priced at no more than $$25,000$ | Priced greater than $$25,000$ | Total |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Sedan | $5$ | $7$ | $12$ |\n| SUV | $4$ | $8$ | $12$ |\n| **Total** | **$9$** | **$15$** | **$24$** |\n\nIf one of the vehicles is chosen at random, what is the probability that the selected vehicle is an SUV and is priced at no more than $$25,000$?"
