      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-305076",
      ":question/problem": "An art supply shop lists $20$ items. The table below summarizes the items by type and whether they are priced at or below $$12$.\n\n| Item | Priced at no more than $$12$ | Priced greater than $$12$ | Total |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Markers | $5$ | $3$ | $8$ |\n| Paints | $8$ | $4$ | $12$ |\n| **Total** | **$13$** | **$7$** | **$20$** |\n\nIf one of the items is selected at random, what is the probability that the selected item is Paints and is priced greater than $$12$?"
